From 43018b6de29cf0e02e7b3f056f178c65f78edb8b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Saiem Amer <saiem.amer07@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 23:26:12 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(orchestration): let a folder-workspace coordinator start
 worktree workers

`orca orchestration worker-start --worktree new-child|new-top-level` looked up
the coordinator terminal's workspace with showManagedWorktree, which has no
folder branch. A coordinator running in a folder workspace therefore failed
with a bare `selector_not_found`, although `new-top-level` never needs the
coordinator's worktree and `worktree create --parent-worktree folder:<id>`
already supports folder parents.

resolveWorkerCreationTarget now handles a folder-workspace coordinator: the
repo comes from `--repo` (a folder has none of its own), a `new-child`
worktree is parented to the folder workspace through `parentWorkspace`, and a
missing `--repo` gets an `invalid_argument` that says what to pass. Worktree
coordinators resolve exactly as before.
